hadiths[31]{hadithnumber,text}:
"21500","Abu Bakr ibn Ayyash narrated to us from Asim from Zir who said: I said to Ubayy: Abdullah says concerning the two refuge-seeking ones. So he said: We asked the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) about them, so he said: It was said to me, so I said, so I say as He said."
"21501","Waki' narrated to us, Sufyan narrated to us, from 'Asim, from Zirr, he said: I asked Ubayy ibn Ka'b about the two Mu'awwidhatayn, and he said: I asked the Prophet, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, about them, and he said: It was said to me, so I said to you, so say. Ubayy said: The Prophet, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, said it to us, so we say it."
"21502","Abd al-Rahman ibn Mahdi narrated to us, Sufyan narrated to us, from 'Asim, from Zirr, he said: Ubayy ibn Ka'b narrated to me, he said: I asked the Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, about the two Mu'awwidhatayn, and he said: It was said to me, so I said. Ubayy said: The Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, said it to us, so we say it."
"21503","Abd al-Rahman ibn Mahdi narrated to us, from Sufyan, from al-Zubayr ibn 'Adi, from Abu Razin, from Zirr ibn Hubaysh, from Ubayy ibn Ka'b, the like of it."
"21504","Muhammad ibn Ja'far narrated to us, Shu'bah narrated to us, from 'Asim ibn Bahdalah, from Zirr, he said: I asked Ubayy about the two Mu'awwidhatayn, and he said: I asked the Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, about them. He said: It was said to me, so I said, and the Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, commanded us, so we say it."
"21505","Affan narrated to us, Hammad ibn Salamah narrated to us, 'Asim ibn Bahdalah informed us, from Zirr ibn Hubaysh, he said: I said to Ubayy ibn Ka'b: Ibn Mas'ud used not to write the two Mu'awwidhatayn in his mushaf. He said: I bear witness that the Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, informed me that Jibril, peace be upon him, said to him: Say: I seek refuge with the Lord of the daybreak, so I said it. Then he said: Say: I seek refuge with the Lord of mankind, so I said it. So we say what the Prophet, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, said."
"21506","Affan narrated to us, Abu 'Awanah narrated to us, from 'Asim, from Zirr, from Ubayy, from the Prophet, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, the like of it."
"21507","Muhammad ibn al-Husayn ibn Ashkab narrated to me, Muhammad ibn Abi 'Ubaydah ibn Ma'n narrated to us, my father narrated to us, from al-A'mash, from Abu Ishaq, from 'Abd al-Rahman ibn Yazid, he said: 'Abdullah used to scrape the two Mu'awwidhatayn from his masahif and say: They are not from the Book of Allah, Blessed and Exalted. Al-A'mash said: And 'Asim narrated to us, from Zirr, from Ubayy ibn Ka'b, he said: We asked the Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, about them. He said: It was said to me, so I said."
"21508","Sufyan ibn 'Uyaynah narrated to us, from 'Abdah and 'Asim, from Zirr, he said: I said to Ubayy: Your brother erases them from the mushaf, and he did not deny it. It was said to Sufyan: Ibn Mas'ud? He said: Yes. And they are not in the mushaf of Ibn Mas'ud. He used to see the Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, seeking refuge with them for al-Hasan and al-Husayn, and he did not hear him reciting them in any of his prayers, so he thought they were two protective supplications, and he persisted in his opinion, while the rest ascertained that they are from the Qur'an, so they included them in it."
"21509","Mus'ab ibn Sallam narrated to us, al-Ajlah narrated to us, from al-Sha'bi, from Zirr ibn Hubaysh, from Ubayy ibn Ka'b, he said: The Companions of the Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, mentioned Laylat al-Qadr, and Ubayy said: I, by the One besides whom there is no god, know which night it is. It is the night the Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, informed us of, the night of twenty-seven, past of Ramadan. And the sign of that is that the sun rises the morning after that night shimmering, having no rays. Salamah ibn Kuhayl claimed that Zirr informed him that he watched it for three years, from the first day Ramadan begins to its end, and saw it rise on the morning of twenty-seven shimmering, having no rays."
"21510","Abu Bakr ibn Abi Shaybah narrated to me, 'Abdullah ibn Idris narrated to us, from al-Ajlah, from al-Sha'bi, from Zirr ibn Hubaysh, he said: I heard Ubayy ibn Ka'b say: The night of twenty-seven is the one the Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, informed us of, that the sun rises white, shimmering."
"21511","And 'Uthman ibn Abi Shaybah narrated it to us, Ibn Idris narrated to us, with its isnad, from the Prophet, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, the like of it, and he added in it: Having no rays."
"21512","Sufyan narrated to us, he said: I heard it from 'Abdah and 'Asim, from Zirr, he said: I asked Ubayy, I said: Abu al-Mundhir, your brother Ibn Mas'ud says: Whoever stands the whole year will attain Laylat al-Qadr. He said: May Allah have mercy on him, he indeed knew that it is in the month of Ramadan, and that it is the night of twenty-seven. He said: And he swore. I said: And how do you know that? He said: By the sign, or by the sign we were informed of, that the sun rises that day having no rays."
"21513","Yahya ibn Sa'id narrated to us, from Sufyan, 'Asim narrated to me, from Zirr, he said: I said to Ubayy: Inform me about Laylat al-Qadr, for Ibn Umm 'Abd used to say: Whoever stands the whole year will attain it. He said: May Allah have mercy on Abu 'Abd al-Rahman, he indeed knew that it is in Ramadan, for it is the twenty-seventh. But he concealed it from the people lest they rely on it. By Allah who sent down the Book upon Muhammad, it is in Ramadan, the night of twenty-seven. He said: I said: O Abu al-Mundhir, and how did you know it? He said: By the sign the Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, informed us of. So we counted and memorized. By Allah, it is indeed it, without exception. I said to Zirr: What is the sign? He said: The sun rises that morning as if it were a basin, having no rays."
"21514","Muhammad ibn Ja'far narrated to us, Shu'bah narrated to us, he said: I heard 'Abdah ibn Abi Lubabah narrating from Zirr ibn Hubaysh, he said: Ubayy said: Laylat al-Qadr, by Allah, I indeed know it. Shu'bah said: And most of my knowledge is that it is the night the Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, commanded us to stand, it is the night of twenty-seven. And Shu'bah only doubted this phrase: It is the night the Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, commanded us. He said: And a companion of mine narrated it to me from him."
"21515","Yazid ibn Harun narrated to us, Sufyan ibn Sa'id informed us, from 'Asim, from Zirr, he said: Ubayy said to me: It is the night of twenty-seven, and it is indeed it, without exception, by the sign the Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, narrated to us. So we calculated and counted, for it is indeed it, without exception."
"21516","Muhammad ibn Abi Bakr al-Muqaddami and Khalaf ibn Hisham al-Bazzar and 'Ubaydullah ibn 'Umar al-Qawariri narrated to me, they said: Hammad ibn Zayd narrated to us, 'Asim narrated to us, from Zirr, he said: I said to Ubayy ibn Ka'b, Abu al-Mundhir: Inform me about Laylat al-Qadr, for our companion, meaning Ibn Mas'ud, when asked about it, used to say: Whoever stands the whole year will attain it. He said: May Allah have mercy on Abu 'Abd al-Rahman. By Allah, he indeed knew that it is in Ramadan, but he liked that they not rely on it. And it is the night of twenty-seven, without exception. I said: Abu al-Mundhir, how did you know that? He said: By the sign the Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, told us: On the morning of Laylat al-Qadr the sun rises having no rays, as if it were a basin, until it rises high. And this is the wording of the hadith of al-Muqaddami."
"21517","Affan narrated to us, Hammad ibn Zayd narrated to us, 'Asim narrated to us, from Zirr, he said: I said to Ubayy ibn Ka'b, Abu al-Mundhir: Inform me about Laylat al-Qadr, and he mentioned the hadith. He said: I said: O Abu al-Mundhir, how did you know that? He said: By the sign the Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, informed us of."
"21518","Abdullah narrated to us, Abu Yusuf Ya'qub ibn Isma'il ibn Hammad ibn Zayd narrated to me, 'Abd al-Rahman ibn Mahdi narrated to us, Jabir ibn Yazid ibn Rifa'ah narrated to us, from Yazid ibn Abi Sulayman, he said: I heard Zirr ibn Hubaysh say: Were it not for your foolish ones, I would place my hands in my ears, then call out: Verily Laylat al-Qadr is in Ramadan, in the last ten, in the last seven, three before it and three after it. News from one who did not lie to me, from news of one who did not lie to him. I said to Abu Yusuf, meaning Ubayy ibn Ka'b, from the Prophet, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him? He said: Thus it is with me."
"21519","Abdullah narrated to us, al-'Abbas ibn al-Walid al-Narsi narrated to us, he said: Hammad ibn Shu'ayb narrated to us, from 'Asim, from Zirr ibn Hubaysh, from 'Abdullah, that he said about Laylat al-Qadr: Whoever stands the whole year will attain it. So I set out until I came to 'Uthman ibn 'Affan, and I intended to meet the Companions of the Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, from the Muhajirun and the Ansar. 'Asim said: He narrated to me that he kept to Ubayy ibn Ka'b and 'Abd al-Rahman ibn 'Awf, and claimed that they used to stand until the sun set, then pray two rak'ahs before Maghrib. He said: I said to Ubayy, and there was harshness in him: Lower to us your wing, may Allah have mercy on you, for I only seek benefit from you. He said: You want not to leave a verse in the Qur'an except you ask me about it. He said: And he was a truthful companion to me. I said: O Abu al-Mundhir, inform me about Laylat al-Qadr, for Ibn Mas'ud says: Whoever stands the whole year will attain it. He said: By Allah, 'Abdullah indeed knew that it is in Ramadan, but he concealed it from the people lest they rely on it. By Allah who sent down the Book upon Muhammad, it is in Ramadan, and it is the night of twenty-seven. I said: O Abu al-Mundhir, how did you know that? He said: By the sign Muhammad, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, informed us of. So we counted and memorized. By Allah, it is indeed it, without exception. He said: I said: And what is the sign? He said: It rises when it rises having no rays until it rises high. And 'Asim that night, from before dawn, did not taste food, until when he prayed Fajr he climbed upon the minaret and looked at the sun when it rose, having no rays until it whitened and rose high."
"21520","Yazid ibn Harun narrated to us, Hajjaj ibn Artah informed us, from 'Adi ibn Thabit, from Zirr ibn Hubaysh, from Ubayy, from the Prophet, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, he said: Whoever follows a funeral until prayer is offered over it and it is finished, he has two qirats. And whoever follows it until prayer is offered over it, he has one qirat. By the One in whose Hand is the soul of Muhammad, it is heavier in his scale than Uhud."
"21521","Muhammad ibn Ja'far and Hajjaj said: Shu'bah narrated to us, from 'Asim ibn Bahdalah, from Zirr ibn Hubaysh, from Ubayy ibn Ka'b, he said: The Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, said: Allah, Blessed and Exalted, commanded me to recite the Qur'an to you. He said: So he recited: Those who disbelieved among the People of the Book. He said: And he recited in it: If the son of Adam asked for a valley of wealth and was given it, he would ask for a second, and if given it, he would ask for a third. And nothing fills the belly of the son of Adam except dust. And Allah turns to whoever repents. And that upright religion with Allah is the Hanifiyyah, not polytheism, nor Judaism, nor Christianity. And whoever does good will not be denied it."
"21522","'Ubaydullah ibn 'Umar al-Qawariri narrated to me, Salam ibn Qutaybah narrated to us, Shu'bah narrated to us, from 'Asim ibn Bahdalah, from Zirr, from Ubayy ibn Ka'b, he said: The Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, said to me: Allah, Blessed and Exalted, commanded me to recite to you. He said: So he recited to me: Those who disbelieved among the People of the Book and the polytheists were not to desist until the clear proof comes to them, a Messenger from Allah reciting purified scrolls, wherein are upright books. And those given the Book did not divide except after the clear proof came to them. The religion with Allah is the Hanifiyyah, not polytheism, nor Judaism, nor Christianity. And whoever does good will not be denied it. Shu'bah said: Then he recited verses after it. Then he recited: If the son of Adam had two valleys of wealth, he would ask for a third valley. And nothing fills the belly of the son of Adam except dust. He said: Then he sealed it with what remained of it."
"21523","Husayn ibn 'Ali al-Ju'fi narrated to us, from Za'idah, from 'Asim, from Zirr, from Ubayy, he said: The Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, met Jibril, peace be upon him, at the stones of al-Mira'. The Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, said to Jibril, peace be upon him: I was sent to an unlettered nation, among them the disobedient old man, and the elderly old woman, and the young boy. He said: So command them to recite the Qur'an in seven ahruf."
"21524","Abu Sa'id, freedman of Banu Hashim, narrated to us, Za'idah narrated to us, 'Asim narrated to us, from Zirr, from Ubayy. Abu Sa'id said: And Hammad ibn Salamah said, from Hudhayfah, he said: The Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, met Jibril, peace be upon him, at the stones of al-Mira', and he mentioned the hadith."
"21525","Abdullah narrated to us, Wahb ibn Baqiyyah narrated to me, Khalid ibn 'Abdullah al-Tahhan informed us, from Yazid ibn Abi Ziyad, from Zirr ibn Hubaysh, from Ubayy ibn Ka'b, he said: How much do you recite Surat al-Ahzab? He said: Some seventy-odd verses. He said: I recited it with the Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, like al-Baqarah or more than it, and in it is the verse of stoning."
"21526","Abdullah narrated to us, Khalaf ibn Hisham narrated to us, Hammad ibn Zayd narrated to us, from 'Asim ibn Bahdalah, from Zirr, he said: Ubayy ibn Ka'b said to me: How much do you recite Surat al-Ahzab, or how many do you count it? He said: I said to him: Seventy-three verses. He said: Never, I saw it, and it used to equal Surat al-Baqarah. And we recited in it: The old man and the old woman, when they commit adultery, stone them outright, as a punishment from Allah. And Allah is All-Knowing, All-Wise."
"21527","Abdullah narrated to us, 'Ubaydullah ibn 'Umar narrated to us, Yazid ibn Zuray' and 'Abd al-A'la said: Dawud narrated to us, from Muhammad ibn Abi Musa, from Ziyad al-Ansari, he said: I said to Ubayy ibn Ka'b: If all the wives of the Prophet, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, died, would it be lawful for him to marry? He said: And what would forbid that to him? He said: I said: Because of His saying: Women are not lawful to you after this. He said: The Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, was only permitted a kind of women."
"21528","Ahmad ibn Muhammad ibn Ayyub narrated to us, Abu Bakr ibn 'Ayyash narrated to us, from 'Asim, from Zirr, he said: I came to Madinah and entered the mosque, and there was Ubayy ibn Ka'b. So I came to him and said: May Allah have mercy on you, Abu al-Mundhir, lower to me your wing, and he was a man in whom was harshness. So I asked him about Laylat al-Qadr, and he said: The night of twenty-seven. I said: Abu al-Mundhir, how did you know that? He said: By the sign the Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, informed us of. So we counted and memorized. And the sign of that is that the sun rises on its morning like a basin, having no rays until it rises high."
"21529","Muhammad ibn Bashshar Bundar narrated to me, Salm ibn Qutaybah narrated to us, Yunus ibn Abi Ishaq narrated to us, from Abu Burdah, from Zirr ibn Hubaysh, from Ubayy, he said: Laylat al-Qadr is the night of twenty-seven."
"21530","Rawh ibn 'Abd al-Mu'min al-Muqri' narrated to us, he said: al-Hajjaj ibn Abi al-Furat, brother of al-Furat ibn Abi al-Furat, narrated to us, 'Asim narrated to us, from Zirr, from Ubayy ibn Ka'b, he said: Laylat al-Qadr is the night of twenty-seven, with three remaining, and he did not raise it."
